// Sequent tests
//
// A sequent is `A_1, ..., A_n ⊢ B_1, ..., B_m` (n ≥ 0, m ≥ 1), putdown
// (⊢ (tuple A_1 ... A_n) (tuple B_1 ... B_m)) - both sides ALWAYS
// tuple-wrapped, even singletons and the empty LHS, so the small-cases
// Rule shapes are uniform across arities.  See the Sequents section of
// lurch-to-putdown.peggy.  The comma-separated sides live only in the
// parenthesized form; the turnstile is the loosest operator of all.

// the bare binary form, all three positive surfaces
A ⊢ B
A vdash B
A proves B
Gamma vdash P

// the parenthesized general form: n = 0, 1, 2 crossed with m = 1, 2
(A ⊢ B)
(⊢ B)
(vdash B)
(⊢ C, D)
(A, B ⊢ C)
(A, B ⊢ C, D)
(A ⊢ C, D)

// the bare prefix form (n = 0 needs no parens standing alone)
⊢ true

// the turnstile is looser than every propositional connective: no
// parens needed around compound sides
A and B ⊢ C or D
A implies B ⊢ C
A ⊢ B iff C

// a LEADING quantifier keeps its maximal scope, so the sequent is
// inside the binding's body (parenthesize the quantifier to make it a
// premise)
forall x. P(x) ⊢ Q
(forall x. P(x)) ⊢ Q

// a bare top-level comma keeps its meaning as the continuation
// shorthand: this is THREE chained assumptions, the last a sequent
Assume A, B, D ⊢ E

// negation requires the parenthesized form (`not` binds a PropArg) ...
not (⊢ false)
not (A ⊢ B)
// ... or the English surface, which ¬-wraps and echoes as English in tex
A does not prove B

// sequents compose as parenthesized operands
(A ⊢ B) iff (⊢ A implies B)

// a single pair premise is distinct from the two-premise sequent (the
// uniform tuple wrapping is what keeps them apart in putdown)
⟨a,b⟩ ⊢ C
(a, b ⊢ C)

// nested sequents must be parenthesized
((A ⊢ B) ⊢ C)

// the subscripted turnstile: provability in a formal system, putdown
// head (⊢ Gamma)
A ⊢_(Gamma) B
A vdash_(Gamma) B
(A, B ⊢_(Gamma) C)
(⊢_(Gamma) B)

// a single-step chain relation is an ordinary expression and may be a
// side (multi-step chains are a targeted error, locked in the error
// tests)
x = y ⊢ P

// a consequence of the bare prefix form: this is not an error but TWO
// LCs, the sequent a ⊢ b and then the prefix sequent ⊢ c, exactly as
// top-level juxtaposition always parses
a ⊢ b ⊢ c
a proves b proves c

// the turnstile glyph is still a mentionable, declarable operator, and
// the word surfaces mention/Declare the same head
⊢ is transitive
(⊢) is transitive
'⊢' is transitive
(vdash) is transitive
Declare ⊢
Declare vdash
